export anchor OscilloscopeStyle:
    number: 309
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Oscilloscope
    idea: The monitor as a bench oscilloscope, phosphor green and yellow traces on a dark graticule with on screen scale readouts, lettered deploy cursors, measurement boxes, knobs and soft keys for the services.
    base: dark
    palette:
        bench: #111315, the page behind the instruments
        body: #1c1f22, the instrument body tone and the style sheet
        panel: #25292d, modules, the knob panel and soft keys
        edge: #3a4046, module borders
        silk: #dfe4e8, silkscreen text
        muted: #a4adb6, labels and name plates
        screen: #040806, scope screens and fields
        graticule: #1f3a28, grid divisions, decorative
        phosphor: #5dff8f, the CH1 requests trace and screen readouts
        yellow: #ffe14d, the CH2 error trace, p95, Degraded, the trigger, the primary button and focus
        cyan: #6fe3ff, p50 and Recovered
        red: #ff8080, Firing
    type:
        Silkscreen in Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, system-ui at 14px,
        and screen readouts in ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas.
        Readouts are 12px mono in trace colours, measurement values 15px
        mono, the incident number 20px mono bold yellow, plate and module
        titles 11px bold caps tracked 0.18em.
    layout:
        A slim black bar holds BRIGHTWORK OPS with Production 24 h
        acquisition and the apps as small tabs with Ops raised. The first
        instrument is a rounded body with a name plate, Traffic scope 2
        channel. Its left part is the screen, a 10 by 8 division graticule
        with centre ticks, readouts across the top for CH1 1,250 rpm per
        div, CH2 0.5 percent per div and time 2.4 h per div, the green
        requests trace and the yellow error trace with a trigger arrow at 2
        percent, dashed cursors A, B and C at the deploys, channel markers
        at left and four measurement boxes below for CH1 max, CH1 min, CH2
        mean and CH2 max. Five soft keys under the screen hold the
        services. Its right part is a 240px column with four knobs for the
        scales and trigger, then a Cursors list of the deploys. A second
        instrument, the module bay, holds a latency mini screen, the
        incident module and a trigger log of alerts. Below 1000px the
        column drops under the screen and modules stack, and at phone width
        soft keys stack and on screen text hides behind the readouts.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px instrument padding, 12px module padding, 24px between instruments.
    density: Medium. One big screen with its controls, then a bay of three modules.
    corners: 20px instrument bodies, 10px modules, 8px screens, 6px keys and fields.
    borders: 1px #3a4046 on bodies and modules, screens inset in black.
    shadows: Deep drop shadows under instruments, a 2px lip under keys, a glow on traces.
    icons:
        16px status shapes on soft keys and log rows, a ringed tick for
        Healthy, a triangle for Degraded, a circular arrow for Recovered, a
        bolt for Firing, a tick for Resolved and a magnifier for
        Investigating. Knobs and cursor letters are drawn, not icons.
    focus: A 3px yellow outline offset 2px.
    tone: Bench instrument terms, such as CH1, per div, cursors, trigger log and acquisition.
